WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Our first guest tonight
is CNN's

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.302 line:92%
chief Washington correspondent

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:03.603 align:start size:94% position:6%
He hosts "The Lead"
weekday afternoons,

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:06.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
as well as the network's Sunda
show, "State of the Union.

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:09.175
Please welcome back to the show,
our friend, Jake Tapper.

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:10.910 align:start size:94% position:6%
How are you, Jake?
-Hey, Seth.

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:11.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
How you doing, buddy?
-Good.

00:00:11.845 --> 00:00:15.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, we talked many times -
you were on the show many time

00:00:15.115 --> 00:00:16.216 line:92%
as a guest during the Trump era.

00:00:16.216 --> 00:00:19.085 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is your first time during
the Biden presidency.

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:23.757 align:start size:94% position:6%
How have things changed
for you so far?

00:00:23.757 --> 00:00:24.657 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Well, it's, uh...

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:29.195
We're still dealing with thing
that Trump left in his wake.

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:32.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
Right?
The failures of his presidency

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:35.068 size:81% position:41%
The pandemic's still
raging out of control,

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:36.703 size:88% position:44%
although there's a light
at the end of the tunnel

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:39.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
with the vaccines,
and then of course,

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:44.711
the January 6th insurrection
the MAGA terrorist attack.

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:48.314 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I wouldn't say
it's over yet,

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:51.751 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, you know,
we also have his legacy,

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:54.421
what he's done
to a once-great political party,

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:58.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
the Republican Party, where,
now a bunch of them think

00:00:58.691 --> 00:01:02.896
that lying and indecency
is the ticket to success.

00:01:02.896 --> 00:01:07.200 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, he's gone, and I'm not -
you know, I don't have

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.869 align:start size:94% position:6%
to pick up my phone
and read tweets

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:12.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
with the same kind
of level of dread

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:16.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I used to have to before,
but he's still --

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:19.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
his presence
is very much with us.

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:21.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, it's like --
What did they say?

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:25.985
You know, "Would you rathe
fight one horse-sized duck

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:29.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
or 10 duck-sized horses?"
-Yeah.

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:30.490 line:92%
-So, we're now fighting --

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:32.759
It's 10 duck-sized horses
is what we're dealing with

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:34.294 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's a Churchill quote,
right?

00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:36.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know you're --
[ Both laugh ]

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:39.165 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Sadie Churchill, yes.

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:42.535
-You've often pointed out
the fact that you become

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:45.839
less popular
based on which party's president

00:01:45.839 --> 00:01:46.973 size:84% position:42% line:92%
is currently in office.

00:01:46.973 --> 00:01:49.876 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have been critical
of President Biden,

00:01:49.876 --> 00:01:52.145 align:start size:94% position:6%
specifically, you know --
one of the things is

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:56.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
his failure to mention
any punishment to Saudi Arabia

00:01:56.850 --> 00:02:00.787
for the murder of the journalist
Jamal Khashoggi.

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:03.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
Why is it important
that President Biden has chose

00:02:03.456 --> 00:02:07.193 align:start size:94% position:6%
not to take any steps afte
this report that was released?

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:09.896 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, he -- I mean,
the main issue here is tha

00:02:09.896 --> 00:02:13.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
he let the Crown Prince,
Mohammed bin Salman,

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:14.534 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
off the hook.

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:16.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's no punishment
for him at all,

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:18.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
even though
the Biden administration,

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:22.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
as opposed
to the Trump administration,

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:25.211
disclosed and revealed
an unclassified statement

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:26.412 align:start size:94% position:6%
revealing that
the intelligence community

00:02:26.412 --> 00:02:30.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
thinks that MBS had this
"Washington Post" journalist

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:32.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
Jamal Khashoggi,
who lived in Virginia --

00:02:32.919 --> 00:02:34.454 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
had him killed.

00:02:34.454 --> 00:02:37.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Biden, as a candidate,
and most of his cabinet

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:41.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
and his administration faulted
Trump for not doing it.

00:02:41.995 --> 00:02:45.498 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know,
in the Bob Woodward book -

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:49.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
I forget if it was
"Fear" or "Rage," or, you know

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:55.008 line:92%
whatever -- whichever, "Fury."

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:58.578 align:start size:94% position:6%
In the Bob Woodward book,
Trump says about MBS,

00:02:58.578 --> 00:03:01.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I saved his ass,"
because Congress wanted

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:04.083 align:start size:94% position:6%
to go after him and punish him
for the murder

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:06.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
of this journalist,
that he ordered.

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:09.689 align:start size:94% position:6%
Biden's basically saying,
"Look, I -- I can't."

00:03:09.689 --> 00:03:12.559
He knows the relationship with
Saudi Arabia is too important.

00:03:12.559 --> 00:03:15.094 align:start size:94% position:6%
Okay, so the words are
different, but either way,

00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:18.998
MBS's ass has been saved
by two presidents in a row

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:21.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I mean, look,
either a president stands up

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:25.271
to a world leader ordering
the murder of a journalist

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:26.973 align:start size:94% position:6%
a "Washington Post" journalist
or he doesn't.

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:29.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just don't see much
of a difference

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:30.710 size:84% position:42% line:92%
in terms of the result.

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:34.214 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What about
the reaction to reporting?

00:03:34.214 --> 00:03:35.748 size:75% position:38%
Is it any different?
Because, obviously,

00:03:35.748 --> 00:03:38.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
any administration
is going to take issue

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:39.385 line:92%
with the way they're covered

00:03:39.385 --> 00:03:42.422 align:start size:94% position:6%
Have you felt
the same level of pushback

00:03:42.422 --> 00:03:46.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
from the Biden administration,
or is it different?

00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:47.794 line:92%
-Not from the administration

00:03:47.794 --> 00:03:49.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think that
they're professionals.

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:52.098 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I think
that Secretary of State

00:03:52.098 --> 00:03:55.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
Antony Blinken, for example --
I think that he understand

00:03:55.668 --> 00:04:00.573
the role of journalists,
and I think that he's not

00:04:00.573 --> 00:04:03.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
gonna personally attack me
or President Biden's

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:04.177 line:92%
not gonna personally attack me

00:04:04.177 --> 00:04:07.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
I certainly don't fear
that Biden's gonna, you know

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:09.482 line:92%
send me some mean tweets.

00:04:09.482 --> 00:04:10.550 line:92%
I mean, I think they're adults

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:12.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
That doesn't mean
I'm not gonna criticize them

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:16.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
or their actions
when I think it's called for

00:04:16.055 --> 00:04:21.027
Now, the left on social media --
Democrats on social media --

00:04:21.027 --> 00:04:24.864 align:start size:94% position:6%
are, you know,
outspoken in their views

00:04:24.864 --> 00:04:29.869 size:88% position:44%
of me criticizing either
Biden or Governor Cuomo.

00:04:29.869 --> 00:04:33.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
They don't like it,
and I've been told that

00:04:33.306 --> 00:04:35.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
some of them
are gonna unfollow me,

00:04:35.408 --> 00:04:37.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
because they -- you know,
I guess they liked

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:39.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
what I did before,
they don't like it now.

00:04:39.212 --> 00:04:40.346 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's okay.
I mean, like I've said,

00:04:40.346 --> 00:04:42.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've been through this
a few times now.

00:04:42.715 --> 00:04:44.751 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
for eight years under Obama,

00:04:44.751 --> 00:04:47.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was a neoconservative
right-wing hack.

00:04:47.787 --> 00:04:49.322 line:92%
Then I was a Trump-hater.

00:04:49.322 --> 00:04:51.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean,
so it's just part of the job

00:04:51.157 --> 00:04:53.426
-You contain multitudes.
I've always said that about you.

00:04:53.426 --> 00:04:55.128 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-I want to ask you --

00:04:55.128 --> 00:04:56.296 line:92%
-Now, that's Winston Churchill

00:04:56.296 --> 00:04:59.032 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughing ]
Yeah, there you go.

